From 802c2dc76fac1210d71e983bafcfecd4f8196b31 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bakhodirovxz <bohodirovasadbek1@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 02:25:27 +0500
Subject: [PATCH 4/8] calc: keep shifted copies unbuilt during a recalculation
 pass

The pass held the tree of every formula it evaluates (`expr_arc`), which for shifted copies would
build all their trees at once and give back the memory they save. It now holds the formula and
builds a shifted copy's tree only while that formula is evaluated.
---
 crates/calc/src/recalc.rs | 45 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-------
 1 file changed, 37 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

